{"id": "EUVD-2026-108839", "enisaUuid": "b8418f54-eb57-319c-a7f3-790cdd7a7d7a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nice: fix use-after-free in dynamic port cleanup\n\nice_dealloc_dynamic_port() uses dyn_port->vsi->idx to erase the dynamic\nport from pf->dyn_ports. However, it frees the VSI before reading the\nindex for the erase, resulting in a use-after-free.\n\nFollow the reverse of the allocation order in ice_alloc_dynamic_port()\nby erasing the xarray entry before freeing the VSI.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c1344df1ae0579f57b97647e5203b06496ce10c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca8a6285b11d01e5a279b1aa7fb55b1a02ecebb1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b98eb58ba2f8fe8e9bba1b8a3b94fa5602c6de84", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1402fc67d2f4e2e1fc7bf8ee0825b8ad994557ff"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99044"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1399289d-2f91-3373-9c19-f4d9798421c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eda69d654c7edae21312f731e0308941cb2ee2a9 <7c1344df1ae0579f57b97647e5203b06496ce10c"}, {"id": "1bf4f737-14c8-33d0-b503-a9418f51975e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eda69d654c7edae21312f731e0308941cb2ee2a9 <ca8a6285b11d01e5a279b1aa7fb55b1a02ecebb1"}, {"id": "326010ee-bf77-33c0-9629-9e91299130ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "695bda54-9a10-3aeb-aa15-7d7dfc87b32a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "7d8ff31c-a4ee-3a75-8d84-71356c0b4681", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eda69d654c7edae21312f731e0308941cb2ee2a9 <b98eb58ba2f8fe8e9bba1b8a3b94fa5602c6de84"}, {"id": "8ed45ce5-27f9-3285-ba3d-2d